      "content": "The acknowledgment of the abyssal vastness of existence can be a crushing reality. The idea that your actions and experiences might be senseless in an ultimately indifferent universe can be a heavy burden. This is often referred to as the \"problem of evil\" - if the universe is uncaring, then how can you find meaning and purpose in your life? This existential despair can be paralyzing, leaving you questioning the value of your existence and the appropriateness of investing emotions and energy in the world.",
      "source": "target",
